Roles
Database Management Systems
Any authorization that can be granted to a user can be granted to a role.
Roles are granted to users just as authorizations are.
Roles can be created in SQL as follows:
create role Assistant_employee;
Roles can then be granted privileges just as the users :
grant select
on courses
to Assistant_employee;

Roles
Database Management Systems
Roles can be granted to users, as well as to other roles:
create role MD;
grant MD to user_name;
Revoking privileges from roles:
REVOKE INSERT, UPDATE, DELETE ON database_name FROM role_name;
Removing roles:
To delete one or more roles, you use the DROP ROLE statement as follows:
DROP ROLE role_name[, role_name, ...];
DROP ROLE role1, role2;

