Database Management Systems
Neo4j - Practice Session
To create a node with properties of different datatype:
Create (x:Book { title:”the lives of others”, author : “Neel”, publisher: [“Chato & Windos”,”w
norton”], price: 285.00, pages : 528, instock : false }) return x
// Creates a node with label Book and 6 properties, where title, author property is of type
string, publisher of type string array, price is of type float, page is of type integer and instock is
of type Boolean.
// creates a node with 6 properties as specified in query
Create (x:Book{details:[“the nagas”,172.00,398]}) return x;
// collections containing mixed types cannot be stored in properties, considering the datatype
of the first value
Create (x:Book{details:[“the nagas”,”172.00”,”398”]}) return x; //Successfull

